<title>USA: Court bars GranCare, Living merger.</title>
<headline>Court bars GranCare, Living merger.</headline>
<text>
<p>ATLANTA, Aug 8 - GranCare Inc said Friday the Delaware Court of Chancery barred its proposed merger with Living Centers of America Inc by granting a preliminary injunction filed by Vitalink Pharmacy Services Inc and Manor Care Inc on Thursday.</p>
<p>GranCare, which announced the $1.8 billion merger with Living Centers May 8, said it intends to immediately appeal the decision to the Delaware Supreme Court.</p>
<p>Manor Care, which owns 51 percent of Vitalink sued GranCare June 17 to enforce a non-competion agreement between the companies entered in February.</p>
</text>
